From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:20:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: clpc: J604 Low Power mode

The J604's ADT (macOS 26.6.2 25G83 and 27.2 26B123) has macOS's Low
Power mode CPU ceiling in the clpc node, cpu-low-power-frequency-max =
2088 MHz. That is a state of the J604's P cluster table; the E cluster
table's first state at or above it is 2172 MHz.

Give T8132 that ceiling on the J604 only, as T6041 has its own on the M4
Max: the low-power platform profile holds every cluster at or below it,
and balanced and performance set no limit. macOS's package power target
in Low Power mode is not measured on the J604, so there is no
low_power_mw and no SMC phandle. Other T8132 Macs are not checked.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c b/drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c
index ff859036c0..3c937be3bb 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/apple/clpc.c
@@ -1500,6 +1500,15 @@ static const struct apple_clpc_hw apple_clpc_hw_t8132 = {
 	},
 	.gpu_demand = false,
 	.gpu_input = true,
+	/*
+	 * The J604's ADT (25G83 and 26B123) has macOS's Low Power mode CPU
+	 * ceiling, clpc cpu-low-power-frequency-max = 2088 MHz, a P cluster
+	 * state; the E cluster stops at its 2172 MHz state. macOS's package
+	 * target in that mode is not measured on the J604, so the profile has
+	 * the ceiling only, as T6041's. Other T8132 Macs are not checked.
+	 */
+	.low_power_khz = 2088000,
+	.low_power_machine = "apple,j604",
 };
 
 /*
